# Tamagui UI — no plain-HTML fallback (umbraculum-dev)

## Rule (hard — MUST)

When authoring or fixing **user-visible UI** under `apps/web/**`, `apps/native/**`, `packages/platform/ui/**`, or `packages/verticals/**/recipes-ui/**`:

1. **MUST** use **Tamagui** primitives (`View`, `YStack`, `XStack`, `H1`, `SizableText`, `Button`, …) and project patterns (`className="brew-panel"`, etc.).
2. **MUST NOT** ship page/section layout as raw HTML (`<div>`, `<section>`, `<h1>`, `<p>`) or ad-hoc inline `style={{…}}` layout as a substitute for Tamagui.
3. If Tamagui fails in a Server Component (`createContext only works in Client Components`, missing theme context): **MUST** add **`"use client"`** (or a small Tamagui client child) — **MUST NOT** rewrite the UI in plain HTML.

## Allowed exceptions (narrow)

- Documented non-Tamagui hosts from [`docs/CODING-STANDARDS.md`](docs/CODING-STANDARDS.md): native `<select>`, `<table>`, `<details>`/`<summary>`, and similar where Tamagui does not apply.
- Middleware / Route Handlers / non-UI modules (no visual surface).

## Canonical patterns

- Web page: `"use client"` + Tamagui — e.g. `apps/web/app/[locale]/(platform-layout)/about/page.tsx`, `HomeAuthenticated.tsx`.
- Human SoT: [`docs/CODING-STANDARDS.md`](docs/CODING-STANDARDS.md) (Tamagui preferred over inline styles), [`docs/TAMAGUI.md`](docs/TAMAGUI.md).

## Agent anti-patterns

| Anti-pattern | Why it fails |
|---|---|
| Plain HTML “just to unblock” RSC errors | Breaks cross-platform UI contract; inconsistent chrome/tokens |
| `maxWidth` / inline styles instead of `brew-panel` + Tamagui stack | Narrow one-off layouts that do not match app panels |
| Mixing a Tamagui shell with large plain-HTML content blocks for new screens | Same MUST NOT — content blocks are UI too |

## Enforcement (umbraculum-dev)

Plugin `alwaysApply` is **not reliably enforced** by Cursor. This repo commits this rule at `.cursor/rules/81-tamagui-ui-no-plain-html.mdc` — agents must treat **this file** as binding.
